    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Salt used in Soap Manufacture: Thomas Mortimer (rev. Dickinson), A General Commercial Dictionary (1823), scan p. 209"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "CAT-SALT: a name given by our salt-workers, to a very beautifully granulated kind of common salt. It is formed out of the bitter or leach-brine, which runs from the salt when taken out of the pan. When the common salt is taken from the boiling-pans, it is put into long wooden troughs, with holes bored at the bottom, for the brine to drain out: under these tr..."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
